 "description": "<p>Nanortalik, formerly Nennortalik, is a town in the Kujalleq municipality in southern Greenland. With 1,337 inhabitants in 2013, it is the tenth-largest town in the country. The name Nanortalik means &quot;Place of Polar Bears&quot; or &quot;Place Where the Polar Bears Go&quot; (from Greenlandic: nanoq). It is the southernmost town in Greenland with a population of over 1,000. Source: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nanortalik\" target=\"_blank\">Wikipedia</a></p><p>For further information (in Danish) see also the Danish Geodata Agency:&nbsp;<a href=\"http://www.gronlandskehavnelods.dk/#HID=5\" target=\"_blank\">Den grønlandske Havnelods</a></p>",
